  "HDDS-11340": {
    "jira_id": "HDDS-11340",
    "issue_type": "Improvement",
    "resolution": "Fixed",
    "title": "Avoid extra PubBlock call when a full block is closed ",
    "description": "Currently, for every client side buffer flush size(32MB default), there will be a putBlock call to DN to persist the block metadata.  For a 128MB block, there will be 4 putBlock calls during the data write, and one extra putBlock at the end when this block is closed due to full.  This last putBlock will add the flag \"eof\" in the request to indicate that this block is completed. \r\nThis task aims to remove this last putBlock call in case this block is a full block when block close is called. ",
